cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Alert-Budget-Aware Evaluation for Transaction Monitoring:
  an evaluation harness for AML models on IBM AMLworld
message: >-
  If you use this software or its findings, please cite it, and cite the
  AMLworld dataset separately — it is a distinct artifact under a different
  licence and is not redistributed here.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thirupallikrishnan
    given-names: Nirmal Kumar
repository-code: "https://github.com/NirmalKumar31/aml-evaluation-harness"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - anti-money-laundering
  - evaluation methodology
  - alert budget
  - class imbalance
  - baseline strength
abstract: >-
  An alert-budget evaluation harness for transaction monitoring, built on the
  IBM AMLworld synthetic benchmark. The alert unit is an (account, calendar-day)
  pair under a fixed daily review budget, which makes every top-k metric
  sensitive to how many candidates and positives a day contains. The harness
  reports each budget metric beside a uniformly random-ranker null, an
  attainable ceiling, and a per-day check that the budget binds, so that a
  published figure can be falsified rather than merely quoted. Under the
  project's own temporal protocol the retained HI-Medium window crosses the
  generator's wind-down, and pooled top-k precision there is driven largely by
  window composition; on the seven-day volume segment a linear baseline finds
  15 positive account-days in 350 slots against a near-zero null. Results are
  reproducible through manifests, replay bundles and a publication gate, with
  content-addressed code provenance and recorded metadata for large data
  inputs. Findings are scoped to one synthetic generator.
